<title>PAKISTAN: World Bank official to steer Pakistan's economy.</title>
<headline>World Bank official to steer Pakistan's economy.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>World Bank vice-president Javed Burki will take charge of Pakistan's Finance Ministry under the newly-appointed caretaker government, a senior government official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Burki, a Pakistani national, will be adviser to the ministry but in charge of finance, economic affairs and planning, the official, who asked not to be named, told Reuters. There will be no finance minister in the caretaker cabinet, he said.</p>
</text>
